//@version=6

// @description TODO: Calculates instant higher timeframe values for higher timeframe analysis with zero lag.
library("CSCMultiTimeframeTools")
// @description The benefits of this formula allow users to gain instant access to higher timeframe values without waiting for higher timeframe sessions to close.
// **REQUIRED** If you use this script in any of your publications it is expected that you credit and link to the originator of the formula,
// The output of this script is very specific and if found in your publication without accreditation, you will be subject to the TradingView House Rules.
// @version 1.0
// @author CoffeeshopCrypto
// author link https://www.tradingview.com/u/CoffeeshopCrypto/

// @function Calculate adjusted lookback period for higher timeframe conversion.
// @param current_tf_minutes Current chart timeframe in minutes (e.g., 5 for 5m).
// @param higher_tf_minutes Target higher timeframe in minutes (e.g., 15 for 15m).
// @param length Base length value (e.g., 14 for RSI/MFI).
// @returns Adjusted lookback period (length × multiplier).

export getAdjustedLookback(int current_tf_minutes, int higher_tf_minutes, int length) =>
    multiplier = higher_tf_minutes / current_tf_minutes
    int(length * multiplier)  // Explicitly cast to int for multi indicator compatibility